{"title":"2010 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 6","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_@MathTalks\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by @MathTalks</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_WhyMath\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by WhyMath</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Which of the following figures has the greatest number of lines of symmetry?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/c/f2cf9516c76e8184d96c3c1686b6d804a2caaa66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\text{equilateral triangle}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"171\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/2/832ab31608615479d5b33e551710ebcb8deb6818.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(B)}\\ \\text{non-square rhombus}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"180\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/d/c1d2929b56e14ef63fa08426fdcce57f364e8f20.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(C)}\\ \\text{non-square rectangle}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"184\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/1/5a1a149e6cbb00006d0ad8e74d63c3082ce70275.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(D)}\\ \\text{isosceles trapezoid}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"168\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/5/5456d1a5e21a263b6bf2d31c6d1bbbbb596daf1f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(E)}\\ \\text{square}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"81\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>An equilateral triangle has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> lines of symmetry.\nA non-square rhombus has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> lines of symmetry.\nA non-square rectangle has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> lines of symmetry.\nAn isosceles trapezoid has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> line of symmetry.\nA square has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> lines of symmetry.\n</p><p><br />\nTherefore, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/0/db01addd15910c55030e045031293ce176fcac16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{ \\textbf{(E)}\\ \\text{square} }$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"91\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_by_.40MathTalks\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_@MathTalks\">Video Solution by @MathTalks</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by @MathTalks\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/RhyRqHMXvq0?si=m1R2q8UnLRD-KksT\">https://youtu.be/RhyRqHMXvq0?si=m1R2q8UnLRD-KksT</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_WhyMath\">Video Solution by WhyMath</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by WhyMath\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/hoZO5M0raTI\">https://youtu.be/hoZO5M0raTI</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?titl